Near miss for comment_swallows_code: banners closed with `*/;` really end
at the `;`, so nothing is hidden. The inert-but-stylistic `*/` tail is
c_style_comment_closer, info tier only, so it appears only under --info
(diag.comment_swallows_code first bullet, diag.c_style_comment_closer).
Suspected issue: the range of a diagnostic on a multi-line comment ends on the comment's first line at column start+token length (past the line's end) instead of at the comment's real end; diag.c_style_comment_closer says "The range covers the comment."
-- input.ssl --
/*******************************************
 Module: shipment label printing
 *******************************************/;
:PROCEDURE PrintLabel;
	:PARAMETERS sShipment;
	/* short note */;
	:RETURN "LBL-" + sShipment;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/*******************************************
 Module: shipment label printing
 *******************************************/;
:PROCEDURE PrintLabel;
	:PARAMETERS sShipment;
	/* short note */;
	:RETURN "LBL-" + sShipment;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:125 info c_style_comment_closer: SSL comments end at ';' - the '*/' before it is literal comment text, not a closer (valid; stylistic)
6:2-6:19 info c_style_comment_closer: SSL comments end at ';' - the '*/' before it is literal comment text, not a closer (valid; stylistic)
